    "order": {
      "group": "classical-apparatus",
      "binding": "forbidden",
      "status": "drafted",
      "rule": "No true classical order, entablature or run of modillions/dentils in any family member. Each member's only contact with classicism is quoted surface ornament carried by a `references` lineage edge with `inherits_kit: false` (dutch-urban-gable-house and flemish-vernacular both quote Antwerp Mannerist / Vredeman de Vries pattern sheets onto an unchanged wall; cape-dutch's late gables quote Louis XVI profiles onto an unchanged wall and plan) — never a structural order.",
      "judgment": false,
      "confidence": "high",
      "note": "Explicitly forbidden rather than left open because all three members' own texts independently make the same point: ornament is quoted onto the wall, the wall and plan 'do not change at all' (cape-dutch), and 'the prints, not the buildings, travelled' (flemish-vernacular, dutch-urban-gable-house)."
    },
